.DS_Store
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
# Revyl ships its agent skills as a CLI-managed package set in .agents/skills,
# linked into .claude/skills. `revyl skill update` owns that content, so a
# vendored copy here would go stale against the installed CLI; reinstall with
# `revyl skill install --cli --claude` instead. Left untracked, they otherwise
# sit in `git status` forever and trip Scripts/check-red-green.sh's dirty-tree
# refusal.
.agents/
.claude/skills/revyl-*
Vendor/
App/Resources/GameData/
App/Resources/woof.pk3
App/*.xcodeproj
App/Info.plist
App/Sources/Generated/
build/
DerivedData/
Scripts/.appstore.env
# Glob, not one literal per destination: ci.yml writes a result bundle per
# test leg (TestResults.xcresult, TestResults-ipad.xcresult), and any one of
# them left untracked makes `git status --porcelain` non-empty, which is
# exactly what Scripts/check-red-green.sh refuses to run against. Adding a
# destination must not silently turn TEST_PROOF into `error` on every pull
# request. See docs/learnings/fixture-stub-trips-own-dirty-tree-guard.md.
TestResults*.xcresult
.testflight-feedback-seen
.superpowers/

# Icon exploration sweeps: 46 MB of generated candidates, superseded by
# Design/source/duck/duck-66px.png. The tools and the chosen artwork's
# reference ARE tracked -- see Design/explorations/README.md.
Design/explorations/2026-*/
Design/explorations/references/*
!Design/explorations/references/ref-01-doom-duck-512.png
